  "title": "Planets around two stars: where can an orbit survive?",
  "subtitle": "5 steps of Planets in Binary Stars (37 in the full investigation)",
  "body": "<p class=\"inv-step-count\">Step 1 of 5 <span class=\"inv-step-kind\">explore</span></p><h3 class=\"inv-step-title\">Run it as it stands</h3><div class=\"inv-step-body\"><p>Open <strong>Binary Planet Run</strong> from the Tools list on the right. It is set to the configuration on screen: the planet starting at 0.15 of the binary separation — 1.5 AU — and twenty binary periods to integrate, which is a bit over five hundred years and about half a minute of watching.</p><p>Press <strong>Run</strong> and watch. The planet goes round about six times a second, so what you can see is not an individual orbit but the band it occupies. Watch whether that band holds its shape.</p></div><p class=\"inv-tip\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">💡</span> Turn the speed down with the transport controls if you want to see a single orbit rather than the band.</p><ul class=\"inv-checklist\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:0\"><span>Watch the trail band: does it stay a ring, or does it start to breathe in and out as the stars swing past?</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:1\"><span>Read \"Integrated\" as it climbs — it counts binary periods, not years</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:2\"><span>Watch the \"Planet’s orbit now\" row: the semi-major axis barely moves, and the eccentricity does not sit still</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:3\"><span>Watch \"Highest eccentricity reached\" — it does not come back down</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:4\"><span>Note the energy drift while the run is quiet; you will want the comparison later</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-check=\"binary-star-planets:run-the-default:check:5\"><span>Let it finish, and read the sentence at the bottom of the panel</span></label></li></ul>",
  "previousDisabled": true,
  "nextDisabled": false,
  "depthState": ""
 },
 {
  "role": "graded",
